 "text": "Tlachtga is a goddess of the Irish and a hill of that land. The name holds the old word for earth. Some tales make her a goddess of the renewal of the year. Other tales make her the child of a wizard. A festival was kept at her hill each summer by the god Lugh. She rode a route in the air above the land.",
